Parents: #8079, #9753
Depends on owner-aware occurrences: #10860
Vocabulary: #9751
Exact identity/query authority: #8168
Reference-family programme: #1667

## One-PR outcome

Project admitted canonical reference occurrences into actual typed execution-owner-to-target edges.

This PR consumes owner identity from #10860 and existing exact target resolution. It does not extract references again, choose roots, traverse the graph, emit diagnostics, or broaden unresolved call inference.

## Admitted initial edges

Project only occurrence classes already exact under canonical facts, including where currently supported:

- direct named subroutine calls;
- explicit package-qualified calls;
- exact static method calls;
- exact coderef captures such as `\&name`;
- exact import/re-export aliases;
- exact typeglob aliases;
- overload coderef only after #1667 provides the canonical reference fact.

Each edge retains owner and target entity/execution-unit identity, occurrence/source/scope/root/generation, edge kind, producer, provenance/confidence/completeness, and invalidation dependencies.

Unresolved instance methods, symbolic dispatch, dynamic coderefs/typeglobs, indirect calls, and unsupported pragma/framework forms remain typed occurrences/boundaries with no fabricated target.

## Compatibility disposition

Inventory the synthetic `ref-source` and other name-derived reference projections. For every consumer record:

```text
migrate to exact owner edge
bounded compatibility projection
non-liveness presentation only
remove
```

Add a mechanical guard that synthetic/name-derived sources cannot feed root-based liveness, exact references, rename, or safe-delete authority.

## Required fixtures

- `root -> _a -> _b` emits two exact owner-to-target edges;
- `_a <-> _b` emits a real cycle;
- top-level and lifecycle owners project edges from their execution units;
- anonymous sub owns its outgoing edge;
- qualified same-name targets remain distinct;
- exact coderef/import/typeglob alias retains projection evidence;
- unresolved `$obj->$method()` emits no target edge;
- same name in another root cannot satisfy the edge;
- stale target or owner generation rejects projection;
- insertion-order permutations produce identical edge identity.

## Negative controls

Fail if:

1. an admitted edge originates from a name-derived synthetic entity;
2. the target is selected by first candidate, display name, range, or map order;
3. unresolved/dynamic occurrences create exact edges;
4. owner, occurrence, source, root, scope, or generation identity is lost;
5. same-name entities cross packages or roots;
6. stale/partial facts become current exact edges;
7. a second reference extractor/resolver is introduced;
8. compatibility projections can enter the liveness graph;
9. graph traversal/root selection is bundled;
10. an edge becomes edit authority by existence alone.

## Codex work packet

Read #10860, #9751/#9753, #8168, #1667, current `EdgeFact`/`EdgeKind`, reference target resolution, and every `ref-source` consumer. Add cycle, dynamic-no-target, same-name-cross-root, and compatibility-guard falsifiers first.

Implementation rule: **exact edge projection plus bounded compatibility guard only. No extraction, roots, SCCs, diagnostics, or edits.**

## Verification

```bash
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo test -p perl-symbol --all-targets --locked facts
cargo test -p perl-semantic-facts --all-targets --locked edges
cargo test -p perl-workspace --all-targets --locked semantic
cargo clippy -p perl-symbol -p perl-semantic-facts -p perl-workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
cargo xtask check-architecture
git diff --check
```

## Acceptance

- [ ] Every admitted edge has exact execution owner and target identity.
- [ ] Dead chains/cycles are representable without synthetic callers.
- [ ] Dynamic/unresolved families remain boundaries with no guessed target.
- [ ] Compatibility/name-derived sources are mechanically excluded from liveness authority.
- [ ] Edge identity is deterministic and generation-bound.
- [ ] No root, traversal, diagnostic, or edit behavior lands.

## Non-goals

No broad method inference, arbitrary dynamic resolution, graph closure, root discovery, diagnostics, or safe delete.

Parent profile: #12176 `compiler_static_project.v1`
Evaluation controller: #12177
Evidence adapter: #12192
Local-profile prerequisite: #12079 / #12157 / #12120
Representative journey authority: #9370 / #7430
Performance/work authorities: #9311 / #9316 / #9321

## One-PR outcome

On one exact candidate, fan in the imported `compiler_local_lexical.v1` result with the current production compiler-world, cross-file navigation, complete cross-file rename, representative-project lifecycle, correctness, work and performance receipts and emit one deterministic `compiler_static_project_cutline.v1` packet.

This PR is proof-only. It performs no world/provider/refactor repair, runs no missing proof implicitly, introduces no new claim row, and grants no support or release authority. Any failed predicate returns to the exact component or instrument owner.

## Required inputs

Consume exact current versions of:

```text
compiler_local_lexical profile/evaluation or bounded #12079-equivalent source packet
compiler_world_currentness_receipt.v1
compiler_world_navigation_receipt.v1
compiler_world_rename_receipt.v1
#9370 representative-project journey and focused #7430 rows
#9311/#9316/#9321 correctness-bound production work/performance evidence
#12125–#12129 target/route/nonzero-work evidence for the selected tests
```

If a source receipt schema is not yet current, the packet is `not_proven`. Do not reconstruct it from issue prose, test names, logs, snapshots, or matching output.

## Exact candidate join

Bind at least:

```text
repository SHA/tree/Cargo.lock/toolchain
perllsp binary/process/package stage where applicable
profile ID/version/digest and imported local-profile identity
project/root/configuration/source generations
ProjectModel/CompilerWorld/fact/provider/refactor policy digests
representative project/fixture identity
receipt producer/schema/tool identities
performance/work policy and measurement identities
```

A same version, same fixture, same output, or same normalized graph from another candidate cannot satisfy the packet. Explicitly reviewed source→package derivation is required where stages differ.

## Required row groups

Retain and evaluate independently:

### Imported local lexical closure

- exact selected upstream and accepted semantic retirement state;
- current accepted parser/semantic/PIR generation;
- live local references and complete-or-refuse rename;
- exact process, work, fallback, mutation and lifecycle rows.

### Static project/world closure

- accepted current ProjectModel/CompilerWorld snapshot;
- compile-time dependency graph and SCC schedule;
- private/public interface transitions and exact invalidation closure;
- stale publication rejection, multi-root and lifecycle currentness.

### Cross-file product closure

- external definition/reference rows from canonical compiler-world facts;
- complete-or-refuse cross-file rename and independent edit application;
- exact producer, subject, source tier, currentness and zero fallback/source-scan work.

### Representative and operational closure

- current representative multi-file journey;
- cold-equivalence correctness;
- production reused/recomputed work separated from oracle/cold cost;
- bounded latency/resource envelope where the manifest requires it;
- nonzero executed test/mutation work and cleanup.

## Verdict and limitations

Emit:

```text
pass | failed | not_proven | stale | invalid
```

`pass` requires every required applicable row and imported lower profile to satisfy the exact manifest contract. An allowed limitation remains visible and lowers the claim ceiling. Missing/instrument-failed/zero-work/cancelled/timed-out evidence is non-pass. Performance cannot compensate for incorrect or stale behavior.

The maximum claim is the exact selected static multi-file/project profile. It excludes bounded EIR/runtime execution, arbitrary dynamic/ambient edges, unselected fact/provider/refactor families, unselected clients/platforms, support and release readiness.

## Falsifiers

Fail when deliberately:

1. combines the local profile from SHA A with world/product proof from SHA B;
2. imports a lower profile by name but not exact version/digest;
3. substitutes a hand-built graph or AST/workspace provider result;
4. lets same output hide a producer mismatch;
5. lets one root/project fill another;
6. drops a failed/unsupported/not-proven row from the denominator;
7. treats a representative journey as proof of an absent focused row;
8. lets performance/work pass hide correctness/currentness failure;
9. counts cold/oracle work as production work avoided;
10. accepts zero selected tests/mutations;
11. reports dynamic/runtime edges as exact compile-time facts;
12. widens the claim to EIR, all providers, all clients or release readiness;
13. produces different normalized bytes on an identical rerun.

## Receipt

Emit bounded private-safe evidence equivalent to:

```yaml
schema_version: compiler_static_project_cutline.v1
profile: {...}
candidate: {...}
imported_local_profile: {...}
world_currentness: {...}
cross_file_navigation: {...}
cross_file_rename: {...}
representative_project: {...}
correctness_and_work: {...}
test_reachability: {...}
limitations: [...]
claim_ceiling: ...
verdict: pass|failed|not_proven|stale|invalid
support_authorized: false
release_authorized: false
```

## Acceptance

- [ ] Every required static-project and imported local-profile row is represented explicitly.
- [ ] All receipts bind one exact candidate/profile/project lineage.
- [ ] Compiler-world currentness, providers, refactor edits, representative proof, correctness, work and performance remain independent.
- [ ] Cross-root, cross-candidate, wrong-producer, zero-work and stale substitutions fail closed.
- [ ] Allowed limitations remain visible and constrain wording.
- [ ] The packet is deterministic, bounded and private-safe.
- [ ] #12192/#12195 can consume it without reinterpreting component semantics.
- [ ] No component repair, profile edit, support pr
